<%# Portfolio dashboard (module 8 part 8.7; PRD §5.4 "Portfolio dashboard (exec/Viewer): all
    projects, CPI/SPI traffic-light cards, current-month cashflow, portfolio-wide forecast").

    THE THREE THINGS THIS SCREEN GETS RIGHT, because each was a measured defect before it:

    1. A BLANK INDEX IS GREY. Not green, not red. On the development database every row of
       v_evm_period has spi_cum NULL and cpi_cum NULL — cost is booked but no baseline or progress
       exists, so no index can be computed. A tile comparing 0 to a 0.95 threshold would have
       painted that project RED, telling the owner it is in breach when the truth is that there is
       nothing to measure yet. `h.spiState`/`h.cpiState` carry 'not-measured' for exactly that.

    2. THE THRESHOLD IS PRINTED. A green tile nobody can check is decoration. The card header
       states the number in force and whether it came from settings or the default.

    3. CLOSED PROJECTS ARE OUT, AND THE PAGE SAYS WHAT IT LEFT OUT. PRD §4.5 excludes each close
       step from a different live view, and says closed projects stay in the history totals
       forever — so there are two labelled figures, live and including closed, never one. The
       toggle names the projects it would add and the step each left at. %>
<% const money = (n) => 'Rp ' + fmt(n || 0); %>
<% const pct = (a, b) => (b ? Math.round((a / b) * 100) : 0); %>
<% const tl = (state, value) => state === 'not-measured' ? 'nt'
     : (state === 'breached' ? 'bd' : 'ok'); %>

<div class="grid k4">
  <div class="card kpi"><div class="lbl"><svg><use href="#i-folder"/></svg>Live projects</div>
    <div class="v"><%= p.totals.live.count %></div>
    <div class="f"><%= p.closedCount
      ? p.closedCount + ' closed, hidden below' : 'visible to you' %></div></div>

  <div class="card kpi"><div class="lbl"><svg><use href="#i-chart"/></svg>Contract value</div>
    <div class="v sm"><%= money(p.totals.live.contract) %></div>
    <div class="f">live projects only</div></div>

  <div class="card kpi"><div class="lbl"><svg><use href="#i-book"/></svg>Cost to date</div>
    <div class="v sm"><%= money(p.totals.live.cost) %></div>
    <div class="f"><%= pct(p.totals.live.cost, p.totals.live.contract) %>% of live contract</div></div>

  <div class="card kpi"><div class="lbl"><svg><use href="#i-in"/></svg>Untagged lines</div>
    <div class="v"><%= untaggedCount %></div>
    <div class="f"><% if (untaggedCount) { %><span class="wn">blocks cost report</span><% } else { %>nothing waiting<% } %></div></div>
</div>

<%# THE CLOSED-PROJECTS ROW. Present whenever there is anything closed, so the live figures are
    never quietly smaller than what the user knows exists. The toggle is a LINK, not a script:
    it works without JavaScript and its state is in the URL, so a bookmark keeps it. %>
<% if (p.closedCount) { %>
<div class="card" style="margin-top:12px"><div class="fbody">
  <p style="margin:0">
    <b><%= p.closedCount %> closed project<%= p.closedCount === 1 ? '' : 's' %></b>
    <%= p.includeClosed ? 'are included below.' : 'are left out of the live totals above.' %>
    <% if (!p.includeClosed) { %>
      Including them would add <b><%= money(p.added.contract) %></b> of contract value and
      <b><%= money(p.added.cost) %></b> of cost.
    <% } %>
  </p>
  <p class="dim" style="margin:8px 0 0">
    <% if (p.includeClosed) { %>
      <a href="/"><b>Hide closed projects</b></a> — back to live figures only.
    <% } else { %>
      <a href="/?include_closed=1"><b>Include closed projects</b></a> — who would be added, and
      why each was out:
      <span style="display:block;margin-top:6px">
      <% p.added.names.forEach(function(n){ %><%= n.name %>
        <span class="dim">(<%= n.steps.map(function(s){ return s.step + ' — left ' + s.left; }).join('; ') %>)</span><br>
      <% }) %></span>
    <% } %>
  </p>
  <p class="dim" style="margin:8px 0 0">A closed project never leaves the history: these figures
    feed future bid estimates. The live totals above simply do not count it.</p>
</div></div>
<% } %>

<div class="card" style="margin-top:12px">
  <div class="card-hd">
    <h2>Projects</h2>
    <span class="r">SPI / CPI breach below <%= p.thresholds.spi %><% if (!p.thresholds.fromSettings) { %>
      (default — not yet set in settings)<% } %></span>
  </div>
  <div class="tw"><table>
    <thead><tr>
      <th>Project</th><th class="r">Contract</th><th class="r">Cost to date</th>
      <th class="r">% spent</th><th>Schedule (SPI)</th><th>Cost (CPI)</th><th>Measured</th>
    </tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <% if (!p.rows.length) { %>
      <tr><td colspan="7" class="dim">No projects are in scope for your account.</td></tr>
      <% } %>
      <% p.rows.forEach(function(r){ %>
      <tr>
        <td>
          <a href="/reports/project?project=<%= r.id %>"><b><%= r.name %></b></a>
          <div class="dim" style="font-size:12px"><%= r.code %>
            <% if (r.exclusion.steps.length) { %>
              · <span class="chip nt">closed</span>
              <%= r.exclusion.steps.map(function(s){ return s.step.toLowerCase(); }).join(', ') %>
            <% } else { %>· <%= r.status %><% } %>
          </div>
        </td>
        <td class="r"><%= money(r.contractAmount) %></td>
        <td class="r"><%= money(r.costToDate) %></td>
        <td class="r"><%= r.contractAmount ? pct(r.costToDate, r.contractAmount) + '%' : '—' %></td>

        <%# One tile per index. The CLASS carries the meaning (ok / wn / nt) and so does the
            WORDS — never colour alone, because this screen is printed and colour is not the only
            way a reader will get it. 'nt' (not measured) is the grey state. %>
        <td><span class="chip <%= tl(r.health.spiState, r.health.spi) %>">
          <% if (r.health.spiState === 'not-measured') { %>not measured
          <% } else { %><%= r.health.spi.toFixed(2) %><% } %></span>
          <% if (r.health.spiState === 'breached') { %><span class="dim" style="font-size:12px">behind</span>
          <% } else if (r.health.spiState === 'within') { %><span class="dim" style="font-size:12px">on plan</span><% } %>
        </td>
        <td><span class="chip <%= tl(r.health.cpiState, r.health.cpi) %>">
          <% if (r.health.cpiState === 'not-measured') { %>not measured
          <% } else { %><%= r.health.cpi.toFixed(2) %><% } %></span>
          <% if (r.health.cpiState === 'breached') { %><span class="dim" style="font-size:12px">over budget</span>
          <% } else if (r.health.cpiState === 'within') { %><span class="dim" style="font-size:12px">on budget</span><% } %>
        </td>

        <td class="dim" style="font-size:12px">
          <% if (r.health.measured) { %>as at <%= r.health.month %>
          <% } else { %>nothing measured yet<% } %>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <% }) %>
    </tbody>
    <tfoot><tr>
      <td><b>Total</b> <span class="dim"><%= p.includeClosed ? 'including closed' : 'what is shown' %></span></td>
      <td class="r"><b><%= money(p.totals.shown.contract) %></b>
        <% if (!p.includeClosed && p.closedCount) { %>
          <div class="dim" style="font-size:12px">closed would add <%= money(p.added.contract) %></div>
        <% } %></td>
      <td class="r"><b><%= money(p.totals.shown.cost) %></b>
        <% if (!p.includeClosed && p.closedCount) { %>
          <div class="dim" style="font-size:12px">closed would add <%= money(p.added.cost) %></div>
        <% } %></td>
      <td colspan="4"></td>
    </tr></tfoot>
  </table></div>
</div>

<div class="card" style="margin-top:12px"><div class="fbody">
  <p class="dim" style="margin:0">
    <b>Reading the tiles.</b> Schedule and cost indices are cumulative, from the latest month with
    a real measurement — the same month the forecast and variance reports use, so no two screens
    describe different months. Below <b><%= p.thresholds.spi %></b> is shown as a breach
    (PRD §4.4). <b>Not measured</b> is grey and is not a breach: it means the project has no
    baseline or no progress recorded yet, and it cannot be on or off plan until it does.
    <% if (untaggedCount) { %>The <%= untaggedCount %> untagged line<%= untaggedCount === 1 ? '' : 's' %>
    block the cost report — <a href="/queue">tag them</a> to make these figures complete.<% } %>
  </p>
</div></div>
